A||||8||DavidHenshaw||Low aspect ratio tires||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||10-07-2000||07:33 PM||||Does anyone know anything about using low aspect ratio tires on the fiero. These are the tires that are only about four inches or so from tread to mounting rim. <P>Dave<BR>86 GT fastback||||reg||1
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||10-07-2000||08:36 PM||||In my V8 Fiero, I have 17x7 wheels all around, with 225/45-17 meats in the back, with 215/40-17 in the front.  They ride/fit pretty good.  Actually, the steering is easier most (likely because of the short sidewall up front) than my 205/55-16 tires on my 87 GT.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-08-2000||10:25 PM||||these are my new wheels.. 17x7(front)(42mm offset) and 17x8.5(rear)(45mm 0ffset) <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-001s.jpg"> <P>215-45 up front and 245-40 out back...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Richard Parnell||10-08-2000||10:55 PM||||How much did those wheels cost you and where did you get them?  They're great looking.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||10-08-2000||11:25 PM||||205/40-ZR17's on mine.  There's about 2 to 2-1/2" of rubber between the road and the rim!  I know, people stare in disbelief, but the sidewalls are super stiff.  I'll admit it's pretty extreme... next time I'll probably bump up to 215/40-17's.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Lower profiles are going to give you a somewhat harder and stiffer "go-kart" type ride.  However, I was suprised that mine weren't as bad as I anticipated, not much worse that the ones on stock Grand Am GT wheels I had on my Fiero before.  It's not too bad, you just have to be pot-hole consious and forget about those fast food drive ups with curbs.  Fast food is bad for you anyway I guess  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DavidHenshaw||10-09-2000||10:48 AM||||Do these wheels/tires improve the fiero's handling of curves. My car is stock and the handling is better than anything I've ever driven but can the low aspect tires make handling better?||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||10-09-2000||01:19 PM||||yes.. as long as you get decent tires.. you get a Toyo Proxy FZ4 and yeah they'll help but not as good as a Proxy T1-S or a Yokohama Nexus or A520. if you looking for SWEET grip stay with a tire with a tread wear of around 200 they will not last 40k maybe 20k maybe (i thrashed a set of A520s in 6000 miles) but they are SUPER sticky! the best real numers wise i've obtained with my former 86 SE was with it's stock 14s and Yokohama A032s on it (DOT approved road racing tire) but the bigger wheels made it ride decent and have a better look to it. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||10-10-2000||01:56 PM||||About the biggest bang for the buck for handling improvement is the addition of a rear anti-sway bar.||||reg||1
Z||000008||the need for speed||10-10-2000||06:55 PM||||I saw a web page that described how to mount your front 7/8 sway bar to the rear and put a new 1 inch up front. my question is that sound like a good idea.can you use the 7/8 old bar and get the same response that a new 7/8 bar would give??just asking becase they look very different. and are they the same length from end to end.better price if you reuse the old one with poly mounts.<p>[This message has been edited by the need for speed (edited 10-10-2000).]||||reg||1
